1
00:00:05,837 --> 00:00:07,259
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,284 --> 00:00:08,835
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:09,861 --> 00:00:11,638
(Episode 10)

4
00:00:47,514 --> 00:00:49,464
Gyu Rim. Han Gyu Rim.

5
00:00:49,489 --> 00:00:50,791
Gyu Rim!

6
00:00:57,567 --> 00:01:00,914
What's this? How much did you drink?

7
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,840
You can't even hold your liquor.

8
00:01:06,323 --> 00:01:07,681
Who are you?

9
00:01:08,998 --> 00:01:10,227
Do you know me?

10
00:01:12,055 --> 00:01:13,243
I'm losing my mind here.

11
00:01:20,185 --> 00:01:21,438
Again.

12
00:01:24,597 --> 00:01:25,858
Get up.

13
00:01:33,573 --> 00:01:36,470
You look so much like Kim Mu Jin.

14
00:01:40,362 --> 00:01:44,559
But a little uglier than Kim Mu Jin.

15
00:01:50,244 --> 00:01:52,877
Thank you. Good night.

16
00:02:45,496 --> 00:02:47,233
Where's my phone?

17
00:02:50,664 --> 00:02:54,744
- What do I do?
- It's in your hand.

18
00:02:55,774 --> 00:02:57,413
Thank you.

19
00:03:04,408 --> 00:03:07,673
- Hello?
- Where are you? Still at the bar?

20
00:03:14,441 --> 00:03:16,383
When Mom walked out on us,

21
00:03:20,507 --> 00:03:22,817
I said I'd go with her,

22
00:03:25,354 --> 00:03:26,817
and she said I couldn't.

23
00:03:28,490 --> 00:03:29,749
Because I was the eldest.

24
00:03:30,332 --> 00:03:33,122
What? I asked if you're still at the bar.

25
00:03:33,147 --> 00:03:35,201
She said since I was the eldest,

26
00:03:36,726 --> 00:03:39,678
I had to look after the others.

27
00:03:46,428 --> 00:03:49,486
That I had to take her place.

28
00:03:50,747 --> 00:03:52,648
Bear it when it's hard,

29
00:03:53,783 --> 00:03:55,573
give in when it's unfair,

30
00:03:56,764 --> 00:03:58,911
yield, understand. That's what she said.

31
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,578
Because I'm the eldest.

32
00:04:02,916 --> 00:04:06,701
That's what the eldest does.

33
00:04:07,792 --> 00:04:09,604
What is this? So annoying.

34
00:04:09,634 --> 00:04:11,184
If you're going to ramble, hang up.

35
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:16,002
Don't hang up.

36
00:04:17,939 --> 00:04:20,088
Don't hang up. Listen to me, you brat.

37
00:04:23,034 --> 00:04:25,060
The eldest, my foot.

38
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:28,589
So I did everything Mom told me to.

39
00:04:29,861 --> 00:04:33,666
Bore it when it was hard, gave
in when it was unfair,

40
00:04:36,295 --> 00:04:38,770
never once did what I wanted.

41
00:04:40,617 --> 00:04:42,361
Even the man I loved...

42
00:04:44,286 --> 00:04:48,444
I gave him up and just lived.

43
00:04:49,139 --> 00:04:50,987
Why are you taking it out on me?

44
00:04:51,012 --> 00:04:52,640
If it's unfair, go take it up with Mom.

45
00:04:52,665 --> 00:04:54,260
Mom's loaded.

46
00:04:54,547 --> 00:04:58,576
Tell her to buy you an apartment,
since you lived like an idiot for her.

47
00:04:58,754 --> 00:05:00,290
Hey, you idiot.

48
00:05:01,023 --> 00:05:03,424
That's not what I meant.

49
00:05:04,030 --> 00:05:06,612
You never get it. So annoying.

50
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,855
Hanging up.

51
00:05:51,347 --> 00:05:53,141
Thank you.

52
00:06:09,297 --> 00:06:11,381
This is so strange.

53
00:06:13,064 --> 00:06:14,209
What is?

54
00:06:16,741 --> 00:06:20,594
You keep looking like Kim Mu Jin to me.

55
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,972
Maybe I really am Kim Mu Jin.

56
00:06:32,841 --> 00:06:36,294
Kim Mu Jin, as ugly as this?

57
00:06:37,787 --> 00:06:39,817
That's impossible.

58
00:06:40,855 --> 00:06:42,961
Why are you insulting my looks?

59
00:06:43,807 --> 00:06:46,578
How handsome could Kim Mu Jin even be?

60
00:06:50,152 --> 00:06:51,741
He's handsome.

61
00:06:53,143 --> 00:06:58,107
Kim Mu Jin is outrageously...

62
00:07:01,632 --> 00:07:03,157
handsome.

63
00:07:09,894 --> 00:07:12,199
So that outrageously handsome man,

64
00:07:13,339 --> 00:07:14,813
why did you break up with him?

65
00:07:14,838 --> 00:07:16,052
What?

66
00:07:19,243 --> 00:07:23,066
How did you know we broke up?

67
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:31,258
Why else would you be drinking alone
and this miserable?

68
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:13,250
You can't just cross like that.
Do you want to get killed?

69
00:08:18,846 --> 00:08:20,603
Why are you talking down to me?

70
00:08:22,267 --> 00:08:25,374
Me? When?

71
00:08:25,664 --> 00:08:29,141
Why do you keep following me?

72
00:08:32,761 --> 00:08:33,953
I'm not following you.

73
00:08:35,054 --> 00:08:36,505
I'm just going my own way.

74
00:08:40,512 --> 00:08:43,990
That outrageously handsome Kim Mu Jin,

75
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,230
did he put you through a lot?

76
00:08:52,144 --> 00:08:53,494
He must've cheated on you.

77
00:08:56,774 --> 00:08:59,554
Did he hit you?
Was it something like that?

78
00:09:02,468 --> 00:09:04,763
Mu Jin would never do that.

79
00:09:05,584 --> 00:09:07,266
You don't know a thing about him.

80
00:09:08,358 --> 00:09:12,386
Still, something must have gone wrong.
That's why you broke up.

81
00:09:13,402 --> 00:09:17,473
Pretend I'm a stranger
and curse him all you want.

82
00:09:20,405 --> 00:09:23,593
Go ahead. It's not like I'll tell anyone.

83
00:09:24,037 --> 00:09:25,683
It's not like we'll ever...

84
00:09:28,514 --> 00:09:33,289
We'll never meet again,
so go ahead and tear the guy apart.

85
00:09:37,436 --> 00:09:39,230
Who are you to call him "the guy?"

86
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,263
Don't talk about him like that.

87
00:09:44,288 --> 00:09:47,293
He isn't someone you get to run down.

88
00:09:50,314 --> 00:09:52,279
He's such a good man.

89
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:56,222
If he's such a good man,

90
00:09:57,257 --> 00:09:59,274
why did he let a woman like you go?

91
00:10:00,154 --> 00:10:03,631
How stupid, how dense, how spineless
does a man have to be?

92
00:10:04,933 --> 00:10:06,884
I'm the one who ran away.

93
00:10:08,901 --> 00:10:15,564
Because I was stupid, dense,
and spineless,

94
00:10:18,462 --> 00:10:20,489
I'm the one who ran.

95
00:10:22,023 --> 00:10:23,520
Why did you run?

96
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:26,933
If he was that good,
you should have held on to him.

97
00:10:27,674 --> 00:10:30,358
No matter what happened,
you should never have given up.

98
00:10:31,069 --> 00:10:33,835
Why did you run? It's driving me crazy.

99
00:10:40,238 --> 00:10:42,556
Why would it drive you crazy?

100
00:10:48,738 --> 00:10:52,850
You're Kim Mu Jin, aren't you?

101
00:11:14,641 --> 00:11:15,836
No, you're not.

102
00:11:17,894 --> 00:11:20,787
You're way uglier than Kim Mu Jin.

103
00:11:26,921 --> 00:11:29,401
The light's green.

104
00:11:34,369 --> 00:11:35,788
Don't follow me.

105
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:42,519
Because of you, I miss Kim Mu Jin so much.

106
00:12:26,057 --> 00:12:27,343
Which way was it?

107
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,913
Which way is my house?

108
00:12:33,491 --> 00:12:34,846
I must be out of my mind.

109
00:12:35,783 --> 00:12:38,548
How much did I even drink?

110
00:12:40,744 --> 00:12:43,252
Snap out of it, Han Gyu Rim. You're fine.

111
00:12:43,404 --> 00:12:44,684
Gyu Rim.

112
00:12:50,726 --> 00:12:52,183
Who are you?

113
00:12:55,003 --> 00:12:57,166
You look really familiar.

114
00:12:57,509 --> 00:12:59,942
Gyu Rim, it's me, Gyu Seo.

115
00:13:00,659 --> 00:13:02,646
I wasn't sure, but it really is you.

116
00:13:03,041 --> 00:13:04,448
You're Gyu Seo?

117
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:09,994
Who are you trying to fool?

118
00:13:10,401 --> 00:13:11,901
You've got three eyes.

119
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,241
My Gyu Seo only has two.

120
00:13:18,161 --> 00:13:22,096
But so many people look alike today.

121
00:13:22,608 --> 00:13:24,603
How much did you drink?

122
00:13:25,121 --> 00:13:26,861
Let's just go home, okay?

123
00:13:26,974 --> 00:13:28,221
We'll talk at home.

124
00:13:34,964 --> 00:13:37,944
I recognize this hand. It's my Gyu Seo's.

125
00:13:38,032 --> 00:13:41,017
We used to hold hands like this
when you were little, didn't we?

126
00:13:41,042 --> 00:13:42,799
I'm glad you at least recognize my hand.

127
00:13:51,514 --> 00:13:52,696
What is it?

128
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:55,587
Nothing. It's nothing.

129
00:13:57,382 --> 00:13:58,563
Let's go.

130
00:13:59,953 --> 00:14:01,313
Walk slowly.

131
00:14:02,504 --> 00:14:03,952
I'm so tired.

132
00:14:06,361 --> 00:14:09,429
- What's so funny?
- No idea.

133
00:14:31,601 --> 00:14:34,884
Drinking herself blackout drunk...

134
00:14:35,138 --> 00:14:41,283
means something huge happened,
something way beyond her control.

135
00:14:41,863 --> 00:14:43,745
What does "blackout drunk" mean?

136
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:45,326
Totally wasted...

137
00:14:46,371 --> 00:14:47,702
You explain it.

138
00:14:48,312 --> 00:14:51,998
It means your mind just goes...

139
00:14:52,819 --> 00:14:54,375
Dad, did you set Gyu Rim off?

140
00:14:55,081 --> 00:14:57,745
What? Am I everybody's punching bag?

141
00:14:58,181 --> 00:14:59,740
Hey, back then, because of you,

142
00:14:59,761 --> 00:15:02,536
don't you remember Gyu Rim losing it
and drinking herself sick?

143
00:15:02,701 --> 00:15:05,042
- When did I?
- Back in middle school,

144
00:15:05,073 --> 00:15:08,277
- you got in with a bad crowd and ran off.
- That was me, actually.

145
00:15:08,364 --> 00:15:10,651
- Was it?
- Gyu Rim drank and was hospitalized,

146
00:15:10,688 --> 00:15:12,815
because Gyu Min
wouldn't attend high school.

147
00:15:12,891 --> 00:15:15,093
Gyu Rim was hospitalized because of me?

148
00:15:15,118 --> 00:15:16,565
Yes, she was.

149
00:15:17,006 --> 00:15:20,334
She got into Dad's leftover bottle
of 45-percent Chinese liquor.

150
00:15:21,392 --> 00:15:22,790
See?

151
00:15:22,815 --> 00:15:25,201
Shake anyone hard enough,
and something falls out.

152
00:15:25,854 --> 00:15:27,295
You too, Gyu O.

153
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:32,141
Out picking fights everywhere you went,
tearing Gyu Rim up inside.

154
00:15:32,234 --> 00:15:36,333
The soju bottles she went through over you
would stack into a mountain.

155
00:15:36,494 --> 00:15:39,681
- That's why I'm keeping quiet.
- Then stay quiet.

156
00:15:40,795 --> 00:15:46,051
The trouble with Gyu Rim
is she drinks with nothing to eat.

157
00:15:46,789 --> 00:15:48,549
She should eat while she drinks.

158
00:15:48,751 --> 00:15:50,208
- Pace herself...
- Come on.

159
00:15:50,233 --> 00:15:54,299
You brat. I'm telling you,
she needs to pace herself.

160
00:15:54,418 --> 00:15:56,900
What is with this family?

161
00:15:57,037 --> 00:15:58,370
We've always been like this.

162
00:16:01,369 --> 00:16:03,754
You guys look like Snow White
and the seven dwarfs.

163
00:16:04,117 --> 00:16:05,580
This one is Gyu Rim's natural enemy.

164
00:16:06,303 --> 00:16:08,631
- Tied for first.
- Whatever.

165
00:16:09,354 --> 00:16:11,401
She's still out? With all this noise?

166
00:16:12,079 --> 00:16:14,361
No wonder.
She was drinking soju like water.

167
00:16:14,386 --> 00:16:15,796
You were drinking with her?

168
00:16:15,916 --> 00:16:19,071
You drank with her and left her there?

169
00:16:19,122 --> 00:16:20,605
I didn't leave her anywhere.

170
00:16:20,687 --> 00:16:23,884
She's the one who wanted to drink.
I left early. I had things to do.

171
00:16:24,309 --> 00:16:25,513
Sure you did.

172
00:16:26,465 --> 00:16:29,044
Busted. Han Gyu Yeong is the culprit.

173
00:16:31,541 --> 00:16:33,358
- Come here.
- Why? I didn't do anything.

174
00:16:33,391 --> 00:16:34,929
Out. Now.

175
00:16:40,789 --> 00:16:42,620
That hurts. Let go of me.

176
00:16:44,923 --> 00:16:46,249
You're bruising me.

177
00:16:46,421 --> 00:16:50,381
Hey, my wedding is two days away.
What if you break my wrist? Then what?

178
00:16:51,072 --> 00:16:52,566
Why was Gyu Rim drinking?

179
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,376
Why are you asking me?

180
00:16:54,401 --> 00:16:55,901
Go wake Han Gyu Rim up and ask her.

181
00:16:56,282 --> 00:16:57,535
Ask her why she drank.

182
00:16:58,221 --> 00:17:00,162
This is driving me crazy.

183
00:17:00,834 --> 00:17:03,894
She's a mess herself,
and I'm marrying into a good family,

184
00:17:03,965 --> 00:17:05,457
so I guess it's eating her up inside.

185
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:06,806
Do you hear yourself right now?

186
00:17:06,857 --> 00:17:08,921
It's a fact.
She's just jealous, I'm telling you.

187
00:17:09,021 --> 00:17:10,284
She's not you.

188
00:17:10,486 --> 00:17:12,663
She's human. She's a woman too.

189
00:17:12,688 --> 00:17:14,090
She has every right to be jealous.

190
00:17:14,406 --> 00:17:17,301
You date that many women
and still know nothing about them?

191
00:17:17,897 --> 00:17:20,002
- Hey.
- She was jealous of me,

192
00:17:20,101 --> 00:17:22,642
so she drank herself under. Happy now?

193
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:27,300
Gyu Rim gave up college because of you.

194
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:30,347
She gave up her own dream
to put you through medical school.

195
00:17:30,701 --> 00:17:33,256
What dream? She never had one.

196
00:17:33,281 --> 00:17:35,152
And I was the better student.

197
00:17:35,441 --> 00:17:38,282
If a broke family can only send
one of us to college,

198
00:17:38,979 --> 00:17:40,301
then it should be me.

199
00:17:41,779 --> 00:17:43,013
Are you even human?

200
00:18:16,497 --> 00:18:19,508
Mom. Why are you crying?

201
00:18:22,037 --> 00:18:23,745
Did you have a sad dream?

202
00:18:28,693 --> 00:18:30,227
Are you thirsty?

203
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:32,024
Should I get you water?

204
00:18:34,301 --> 00:18:37,484
Feeling sick? Should I get you medicine?

205
00:18:44,621 --> 00:18:46,031
Not medicine.

206
00:18:47,375 --> 00:18:49,248
Just hug me, Gyeol.

207
00:18:50,218 --> 00:18:52,733
- Yeah?
- Come here, my boy.

208
00:18:59,858 --> 00:19:01,071
I'm sorry.

209
00:19:02,206 --> 00:19:06,458
I'm so sorry I worried you, sweetheart.

210
00:19:07,538 --> 00:19:12,848
It'll never happen again.
I'm sorry, Gyeol.

211
00:19:13,291 --> 00:19:16,405
It's okay, Mom.

212
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:38,967
Don't hang up. Listen to me, you brat.
The eldest, my foot.

213
00:19:39,161 --> 00:19:41,826
So I did everything Mom told me to.

214
00:19:42,127 --> 00:19:45,361
Bore it when it was hard,
gave in when it was unfair,

215
00:19:45,565 --> 00:19:47,902
never once did what I wanted,

216
00:19:48,625 --> 00:19:50,345
even the man I loved...

217
00:19:51,949 --> 00:19:55,439
I gave him up and just lived.

218
00:20:17,523 --> 00:20:18,982
You spent the night out here?

219
00:20:21,681 --> 00:20:23,855
Your place is a short walk from here.

220
00:20:24,706 --> 00:20:28,866
You sure know how to worry people
in all sorts of creative ways.

221
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:33,723
So why didn't you pick up?

222
00:20:33,979 --> 00:20:36,792
It rang fine,
so it's not a problem with the phone.

223
00:20:38,134 --> 00:20:41,427
Your fingers work fine.
Why didn't you answer? I was worried.

224
00:20:41,728 --> 00:20:43,008
You're killing me!

225
00:20:45,041 --> 00:20:46,698
Who am I even talking to?

226
00:20:48,319 --> 00:20:49,547
Right now, at the house,

227
00:20:51,442 --> 00:20:53,253
there's a guest.

228
00:20:53,967 --> 00:20:56,346
- What?
- You haven't eaten, have you?

229
00:20:57,114 --> 00:21:01,071
I'll quietly get out of your way.
Enjoy getting cursed out over breakfast.

230
00:21:01,184 --> 00:21:03,896
There's antacid in the fridge. Take some.

231
00:21:05,984 --> 00:21:08,216
Are you my son or my friend?

232
00:21:14,902 --> 00:21:16,095
A guest?

233
00:21:38,842 --> 00:21:40,471
Did you date a gold digger?

234
00:21:42,104 --> 00:21:44,778
- Sorry?
- That's what your mother said.

235
00:21:46,486 --> 00:21:49,170
That the woman you dated
was a gold digger.

236
00:21:55,972 --> 00:21:57,470
She was nothing like that.

237
00:22:03,341 --> 00:22:04,865
I heard otherwise.

238
00:22:06,275 --> 00:22:08,189
Dirt-poor family,

239
00:22:09,377 --> 00:22:11,719
no college, and a string of siblings.

240
00:22:14,861 --> 00:22:18,805
Is there something wrong with being poor
or not going to college?

241
00:22:19,009 --> 00:22:22,578
Of everyone I have ever known,

242
00:22:22,987 --> 00:22:27,238
she is the wisest, smartest,
most decent and strongest woman.

243
00:22:27,341 --> 00:22:30,065
She's a far finer person
than someone like me could ever be.

244
00:22:30,761 --> 00:22:32,423
Then why did you break up?

245
00:22:34,454 --> 00:22:36,980
Why did you leave a girl that fine?

246
00:22:38,044 --> 00:22:39,758
Did you break up
because your mother told you to?

247
00:22:42,625 --> 00:22:44,240
Or did you think it over...

248
00:22:45,156 --> 00:22:47,115
and decide dating was fine,

249
00:22:48,103 --> 00:22:51,069
but marriage wasn't realistic,
so you ended it?

250
00:22:52,407 --> 00:22:53,697
Let's stop talking about her.

251
00:22:55,225 --> 00:22:57,990
Neither you nor I, nor anyone else,

252
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:01,809
has any right to speak of her that way.

253
00:23:03,161 --> 00:23:05,740
If you think I'm not good enough
for Seo Hyeon,

254
00:23:05,846 --> 00:23:07,771
then blame me and me alone.

255
00:23:07,989 --> 00:23:10,844
Why date her at all
if it was going to end like this?

256
00:23:12,684 --> 00:23:15,427
Why date her
if you couldn't take responsibility?

257
00:23:16,149 --> 00:23:19,062
Why date her if you couldn't protect her?

258
00:23:24,275 --> 00:23:25,737
You may be...

259
00:23:27,221 --> 00:23:30,258
as remarkable and impressive as they come,

260
00:23:30,507 --> 00:23:31,782
but to a household like yours,

261
00:23:32,672 --> 00:23:38,134
one that tramples people
and lords rank over them,

262
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:39,807
I refuse to give Seo Hyeon,

263
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:43,783
my own daughter.

264
00:23:45,941 --> 00:23:48,827
So please, let this go here, Mu Jin.

265
00:24:04,574 --> 00:24:05,846
Maybe it's because...

266
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:09,471
I'm raising a daughter myself,

267
00:24:09,863 --> 00:24:12,395
but that girl keeps weighing on me.

268
00:24:14,701 --> 00:24:19,548
Treated like a gold digger by your family,

269
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:23,933
bearing all that hurt and humiliation,

270
00:24:26,334 --> 00:24:28,184
how did she ever walk away from you?

271
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:46,153
What? Not even over her dead body?

272
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:50,255
Some woman who came out of nowhere,

273
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:53,813
I treated her like the chairman's wife,
and she forgets her place.

274
00:24:54,341 --> 00:24:57,006
She was their housekeeper, wasn't she?

275
00:24:57,101 --> 00:24:58,365
Exactly.

276
00:24:59,131 --> 00:25:02,491
She must've worked her charms
on Chairman Jang after he lost his wife,

277
00:25:02,558 --> 00:25:06,030
then charmed Seo Hyeon
and moved into that house.

278
00:25:06,061 --> 00:25:07,199
A woman with no pedigree.

279
00:25:07,501 --> 00:25:11,662
Seo Hyeon adores her so much that
strangers think she gave birth to her.

280
00:25:12,183 --> 00:25:16,069
Should I kidnap that little thing
and dump her out in a desert?

281
00:25:16,347 --> 00:25:18,979
Just until Mu Jin
and Seo Hyeon's wedding is over?

282
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:25,733
Why do you even want to be in-laws
with that woman, Mom?

283
00:25:26,547 --> 00:25:29,632
Is it for her? It's for Chairman Jang.

284
00:25:30,161 --> 00:25:35,295
How did a family like the Jangs
ever allow that remarriage?

285
00:25:35,371 --> 00:25:36,752
To a housekeeper, no less.

286
00:25:36,777 --> 00:25:39,320
Nobody bends Chairman Jang's will.

287
00:25:40,067 --> 00:25:43,268
Chairman Jang is exactly like Mu Jin.

288
00:25:43,964 --> 00:25:48,758
Once it catches his eye, he's blind.
Trying to stop him only makes it worse.

289
00:25:52,281 --> 00:25:55,392
I'm sorry. He insisted on seeing you.

290
00:25:55,422 --> 00:25:57,172
What did you say to Gyu Rim?

291
00:25:58,480 --> 00:26:00,006
Secretary Kim, step outside.

292
00:26:01,819 --> 00:26:04,877
Did you call Gyu Rim a gold digger?

293
00:26:05,851 --> 00:26:08,069
Why Gyu Rim again, and not Seo Hyeon?

294
00:26:08,127 --> 00:26:09,895
Why is she coming up again?

295
00:26:10,087 --> 00:26:12,328
I asked if you called her a gold digger.

296
00:26:12,713 --> 00:26:15,392
Who? Who said that?

297
00:26:16,010 --> 00:26:17,450
Did Seo Hyeon's mother tell you?

298
00:26:18,246 --> 00:26:20,491
Why is that woman stirring up trouble?

299
00:26:20,516 --> 00:26:21,918
What is she after?

300
00:26:22,614 --> 00:26:24,426
How is Gyu Rim a gold digger?

301
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:26,496
Why are you smearing her?

302
00:26:27,501 --> 00:26:29,214
You think gold diggers
are some other breed?

303
00:26:29,719 --> 00:26:34,404
Seducing a man out of her league.
That's a gold digger.

304
00:26:34,429 --> 00:26:35,607
Mother.

305
00:26:37,858 --> 00:26:42,048
Yun Jin, this one has completely lost it.

306
00:26:42,347 --> 00:26:44,949
He might actually take a swing at me.

307
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,223
Why drag up something long finished?

308
00:26:47,381 --> 00:26:51,232
Her head is already splitting
over the Seo Hyeon situation.

309
00:26:51,257 --> 00:26:52,878
You said you did nothing.

310
00:26:54,009 --> 00:26:56,224
You said you did nothing to Gyu Rim.

311
00:26:56,249 --> 00:26:57,871
We did nothing.

312
00:26:57,988 --> 00:27:01,991
What would we do?
We never laid a finger on her.

313
00:27:04,956 --> 00:27:06,995
Did you and Mom play me?

314
00:27:07,054 --> 00:27:08,542
What are you talking about?

315
00:27:08,882 --> 00:27:12,491
Han Gyu Rim recorded herself asking
for 100,000 dollars to leave you...

316
00:27:17,733 --> 00:27:19,905
Gyu Rim recorded that and handed it over?

317
00:27:21,737 --> 00:27:23,605
No, that's not it.

318
00:27:24,367 --> 00:27:25,884
She wanted you to play that for me?

319
00:27:26,735 --> 00:27:28,655
So I would give her up?

320
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:31,663
And then she left? Gyu Rim did?

321
00:27:32,284 --> 00:27:36,305
- No, that's not...
- If it isn't,

322
00:27:36,719 --> 00:27:39,169
did Gyu Rim really take
100,000 dollars from you?

323
00:27:45,712 --> 00:27:47,324
Yun Jin, get out of the way.

324
00:27:47,441 --> 00:27:49,884
If that fist lands on you,
we'll be holding your funeral today.

325
00:27:49,909 --> 00:27:51,045
Move, now.

326
00:27:51,521 --> 00:27:54,203
Fine. Hit me if you want to.

327
00:27:56,153 --> 00:28:00,203
If hitting me brings you to your senses,
I'll take as many as you want.

328
00:28:05,724 --> 00:28:06,911
So what will you do?

329
00:28:07,947 --> 00:28:11,213
Dump Seo Hyeon and run to Gyu Rim?

330
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:16,982
I hear you held Seo Hyeon back
when she tried to leave.

331
00:28:17,329 --> 00:28:21,457
You made one woman weep blood once.
Don't you dare do it again.

332
00:28:22,241 --> 00:28:26,398
Don't you know a woman's grudge
can freeze the hottest day of summer?

333
00:29:01,071 --> 00:29:02,360
Should I heat it again?

334
00:29:05,594 --> 00:29:08,700
I love that you're not picky
and you'll eat anything.

335
00:29:14,521 --> 00:29:17,818
I even made you hangover soup.

336
00:29:17,980 --> 00:29:19,340
Pretty touching, isn't it?

337
00:29:19,681 --> 00:29:21,011
If you're touched, that'll be fifty cents.

338
00:29:23,929 --> 00:29:25,359
Seven years ago,

339
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:28,980
I got Mom's number from her friend,

340
00:29:30,225 --> 00:29:32,342
and I called her once.

341
00:29:35,903 --> 00:29:37,284
What did you call her for?

342
00:29:38,473 --> 00:29:42,816
She remarried well,
cut off her children and me,

343
00:29:43,804 --> 00:29:46,173
and lives happily. A heartless woman.

344
00:29:48,221 --> 00:29:50,605
I told her I was struggling so much...

345
00:29:55,361 --> 00:29:56,979
and asked her to come just once.

346
00:30:00,319 --> 00:30:05,108
I told her I missed her so much,

347
00:30:07,125 --> 00:30:09,116
but her daughter had appendix surgery.

348
00:30:11,227 --> 00:30:15,004
She said she was sorry,
but she couldn't come.

349
00:30:16,150 --> 00:30:17,192
What?

350
00:30:23,094 --> 00:30:25,219
After that, I blocked her number.

351
00:30:27,344 --> 00:30:30,344
Good. That cold-hearted woman.

352
00:30:32,177 --> 00:30:35,876
She always was sharp and cold like that.

353
00:30:38,839 --> 00:30:40,861
Have some more.

354
00:30:42,858 --> 00:30:45,821
- I can't stand the sight of you either.
- What?

355
00:30:49,415 --> 00:30:50,498
I think I'm going to be sick.

356
00:30:51,356 --> 00:30:54,719
What? Hey.

357
00:30:57,777 --> 00:30:59,263
What just happened here?

358
00:30:59,719 --> 00:31:02,518
Hey, walking off like that really hurts.

359
00:31:04,096 --> 00:31:06,612
A woman's heart is impossible to read.

360
00:31:38,719 --> 00:31:40,427
(Jeong Woo)

361
00:31:42,352 --> 00:31:43,436
Hello.

362
00:31:43,692 --> 00:31:47,063
Where are you? I'm asking you.

363
00:31:51,267 --> 00:31:52,552
Outside Gyu Rim's place.

364
00:31:53,044 --> 00:31:56,095
Are you crazy? Why are you there?

365
00:31:57,067 --> 00:31:59,778
Right. Why did I come here?

366
00:32:00,094 --> 00:32:01,511
Did your car drive itself there?

367
00:32:02,219 --> 00:32:05,839
Forget it. Start the car, set the GPS
for the restaurant, and get here now.

368
00:32:06,261 --> 00:32:07,999
If you can't drive, I'll come to you.

369
00:32:08,419 --> 00:32:12,006
No, I'll come.
I'm heading to the shop now.

370
00:32:30,721 --> 00:32:32,471
Yes, I'm all right now, Su Nam.

371
00:32:32,496 --> 00:32:33,795
I'm walking out the gate now.

372
00:32:33,962 --> 00:32:35,469
Yes, see you soon.

373
00:33:06,483 --> 00:33:09,620
ID, check. Cards, check...

374
00:33:11,036 --> 00:33:13,333
Cash, too. It's all here.

375
00:33:37,642 --> 00:33:38,927
You okay, Gyu Rim?

376
00:33:40,784 --> 00:33:42,723
- Did you lose something?
- Yes.

377
00:33:42,943 --> 00:33:44,011
What is it?

378
00:33:50,782 --> 00:33:52,687
Dad, lift your foot, please.

379
00:33:53,929 --> 00:33:57,028
Don't talk to me. I'm deeply hurt.

380
00:33:58,055 --> 00:34:01,075
How could you, of all people,
say that to me, your own father?

381
00:34:16,372 --> 00:34:18,284
Hey, you brat!

382
00:34:20,741 --> 00:34:21,783
What?

383
00:34:22,719 --> 00:34:24,793
There's nothing under Dad's foot, Gyu Rim.

384
00:34:25,027 --> 00:34:29,657
Hey, I said I'm deeply hurt.
Don't talk to me.

385
00:34:29,844 --> 00:34:32,665
I didn't talk. I just lifted your foot.

386
00:34:34,634 --> 00:34:35,898
You hit hard.

387
00:34:48,722 --> 00:34:51,239
What is it? What did you lose?

388
00:34:52,427 --> 00:34:56,202
Money? Your ID? Your cards?

389
00:34:56,290 --> 00:34:58,268
No, I have all of that.

390
00:34:58,886 --> 00:35:02,253
Then what? I need to know to help you.

391
00:35:03,011 --> 00:35:04,520
That's the thing.

392
00:35:05,511 --> 00:35:07,207
I don't know what it is.

393
00:35:07,886 --> 00:35:10,324
I definitely lost something, but...

394
00:35:11,719 --> 00:35:14,135
I can't figure out what it was.

395
00:35:16,310 --> 00:35:19,401
Still hungover? Want me to get medicine?

396
00:35:23,427 --> 00:35:25,841
(Kkokko Byeol Bar)

397
00:35:59,469 --> 00:36:00,907
What is all this?

398
00:36:01,007 --> 00:36:04,190
You're here. What do you think?

399
00:36:04,288 --> 00:36:09,530
My little celebration for Gyu Rim
and Cho Heung Sik's fresh start.

400
00:36:09,677 --> 00:36:11,264
Buy one, get one free.

401
00:36:14,597 --> 00:36:16,571
How are you feeling, though?

402
00:36:16,843 --> 00:36:19,942
When your stomach's off, you have to rest.

403
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:23,401
Heung Sik hasn't even said yes yet...

404
00:36:24,219 --> 00:36:28,193
Let's celebrate once he accepts
and it's all settled.

405
00:36:29,177 --> 00:36:32,907
We don't need that brat's opinion.

406
00:36:33,052 --> 00:36:37,219
If I say yes, he says yes automatically.

407
00:36:38,177 --> 00:36:39,219
Still.

408
00:36:40,261 --> 00:36:41,721
Stubborn thing.

409
00:36:41,886 --> 00:36:44,677
Fine.

410
00:36:45,777 --> 00:36:48,361
I'll head over right now,

411
00:36:48,386 --> 00:36:52,901
feed him his favorite pork bone stew,
and bring back his yes, right?

412
00:36:54,344 --> 00:36:57,064
But what to do?

413
00:36:57,386 --> 00:37:01,251
Mr. Oh from Majang Dong comes at 2:30,

414
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:03,848
and I completely forgot.

415
00:37:03,969 --> 00:37:05,819
Then I'll go see Heung Sik myself.

416
00:37:05,844 --> 00:37:07,427
Would you? All right.

417
00:37:07,844 --> 00:37:10,799
That works out perfectly for me.

418
00:37:11,177 --> 00:37:12,969
Heung Sik will be over the moon.

419
00:37:15,033 --> 00:37:16,212
I'll be back.

420
00:37:16,712 --> 00:37:19,612
- Go on, hurry back.
- Yes.

421
00:37:21,677 --> 00:37:23,693
This worked out well.

422
00:37:33,636 --> 00:37:37,383
Heung Sik, food's ready. Let's eat.

423
00:37:41,601 --> 00:37:42,867
Heung Sik.

424
00:37:43,715 --> 00:37:46,091
The pork bone stew came out great.

425
00:37:46,917 --> 00:37:48,012
Stop.

426
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:51,034
Just how close are you planning to get?

427
00:37:51,757 --> 00:37:53,209
Aren't you going to eat?

428
00:37:54,636 --> 00:37:56,415
I'm not letting you feed me.

429
00:37:57,136 --> 00:37:58,192
Why not?

430
00:38:00,275 --> 00:38:04,942
When you're close, I can't breathe right,

431
00:38:05,125 --> 00:38:08,803
and my heart races too fast.
Just don't come near me.

432
00:38:10,158 --> 00:38:12,286
You've always had arrhythmia.

433
00:38:13,527 --> 00:38:14,996
All the more reason, then.

434
00:38:15,427 --> 00:38:17,427
Leave it, and I'll manage on my own.

435
00:38:17,452 --> 00:38:20,652
How? You can't use your arm.

436
00:38:22,719 --> 00:38:25,646
- I'll have Gyu O come.
- Gyu O has plans today.

437
00:38:27,261 --> 00:38:28,778
Then I'll have my mother come.

438
00:38:29,177 --> 00:38:31,240
Su Nam has plans today.

439
00:38:36,589 --> 00:38:39,988
Is it still happening? Can't you breathe?

440
00:38:40,761 --> 00:38:42,246
Should I check your pulse?

441
00:38:45,261 --> 00:38:47,364
Hold on.

442
00:38:49,969 --> 00:38:51,427
Fine, I'm going.

443
00:38:51,677 --> 00:38:53,318
I'm leaving, so relax.

444
00:38:57,059 --> 00:39:00,694
I must look like a madman.

445
00:39:03,422 --> 00:39:05,372
I'm not exactly normal either.

446
00:39:07,677 --> 00:39:10,136
I lost something yesterday,

447
00:39:11,469 --> 00:39:13,176
and I don't know what it was.

448
00:39:15,172 --> 00:39:19,200
No matter how hard I think,
it just won't come to me.

449
00:39:20,658 --> 00:39:21,658
Is that so?

450
00:39:52,302 --> 00:39:53,636
(Dad)

451
00:40:03,373 --> 00:40:06,206
I hear you fought a patient and got fired.

452
00:40:11,365 --> 00:40:14,001
How do you know? Who told you?

453
00:40:15,540 --> 00:40:18,477
I went by your clinic
and heard it from a nurse. Why?

454
00:40:19,136 --> 00:40:21,187
Why would you go there?

455
00:40:21,275 --> 00:40:23,042
For a facial, obviously.

456
00:40:23,094 --> 00:40:25,026
Your wedding is right around the corner.

457
00:40:25,478 --> 00:40:29,452
A leopard doesn't change its spots.
Now you're fighting patients?

458
00:40:29,743 --> 00:40:32,373
What business is it of yours that I fight?

459
00:40:32,525 --> 00:40:35,177
You've turned into a brawler. Trouble.

460
00:40:35,546 --> 00:40:37,783
You'll start a fight with me
right in the middle of the aisle.

461
00:40:37,969 --> 00:40:39,444
Your comeback is canceled.

462
00:40:39,469 --> 00:40:41,959
- You don't need to come to the wedding.
- What?

463
00:40:42,302 --> 00:40:45,136
Dad, let's just go back to you being dead.

464
00:40:45,718 --> 00:40:47,147
You can't do that.

465
00:40:47,237 --> 00:40:49,430
You didn't keep your promise either.

466
00:40:49,455 --> 00:40:52,856
I asked you to split up Cho Heung Sik
and Han Gyu Rim, and now they're dating?

467
00:40:52,927 --> 00:40:55,864
So you kill me off, revive me,
and kill me off again?

468
00:40:55,889 --> 00:40:58,748
What am I, a frozen fish?
Freeze, thaw, freeze again?

469
00:40:59,677 --> 00:41:03,361
You should have lived right
in the first place.

470
00:41:03,386 --> 00:41:07,094
You didn't have to make me proud,
but you didn't have to shame me.

471
00:41:07,119 --> 00:41:08,341
Hey, did you two plan this?

472
00:41:09,219 --> 00:41:11,471
Did you and Gyu Rim plan this? Hey.

473
00:41:12,194 --> 00:41:15,021
You think I lived my life this way
because I wanted to?

474
00:41:15,219 --> 00:41:17,142
This is so unfair...

475
00:41:18,352 --> 00:41:20,186
What did I do that was so wrong?

476
00:41:20,211 --> 00:41:21,506
(Chairman Jang)

477
00:41:24,485 --> 00:41:27,185
Don't tell the family I quit medicine.

478
00:41:27,268 --> 00:41:29,999
Above all, never tell Han Gyu Rim.
Do you understand...

479
00:41:40,263 --> 00:41:41,390
Hello, Chairman Jang.

480
00:42:00,073 --> 00:42:01,316
What are you doing?

481
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:05,995
Ma'am.

482
00:42:06,339 --> 00:42:08,516
Trying to drown yourself in that dish?

483
00:42:09,797 --> 00:42:11,123
How did you know?

484
00:42:17,562 --> 00:42:19,728
You have a talent for comedy.

485
00:42:19,972 --> 00:42:21,709
Do I look like I'm joking right now?

486
00:42:21,734 --> 00:42:24,877
So you're really, truly trying to die?

487
00:42:25,719 --> 00:42:29,003
If you hadn't shown up,
I really could have died.

488
00:42:30,692 --> 00:42:32,282
Did something happen?

489
00:42:34,438 --> 00:42:37,020
Something that made me want
to drown myself in that dish.

490
00:42:39,386 --> 00:42:40,581
Trouble with your wife?

491
00:42:42,790 --> 00:42:44,082
I don't have a wife.

492
00:42:44,380 --> 00:42:45,687
Trouble with your children?

493
00:42:50,558 --> 00:42:52,183
Pour me one too.

494
00:42:52,344 --> 00:42:53,927
One soju glass over here...

495
00:42:54,219 --> 00:42:55,890
No, make it a bottle of soju.

496
00:42:55,969 --> 00:42:57,719
A glass won't cut it today.

497
00:42:57,761 --> 00:42:59,512
I'm drinking straight from the bottle.

498
00:42:59,802 --> 00:43:03,808
Drink from a glass.
It's bad for your health. Even I...

499
00:43:05,845 --> 00:43:09,434
I drink from a glass for my health, see?

500
00:43:16,219 --> 00:43:19,026
Want to bet whose child is worse?

501
00:43:20,469 --> 00:43:23,607
- You're on.
- You go first.

502
00:43:25,261 --> 00:43:29,488
I even made my eldest hangover soup.

503
00:43:30,055 --> 00:43:33,262
She says she can't stand the sight of me.
Says I make her sick.

504
00:43:35,690 --> 00:43:37,719
My one and only son,

505
00:43:39,221 --> 00:43:42,457
I lost my husband early
and raised him like a treasure.

506
00:43:44,261 --> 00:43:47,149
He walked out on me
and left home over a woman.

507
00:43:48,034 --> 00:43:51,472
He shows up today after years away,
and takes that girl's side...

508
00:43:51,497 --> 00:43:53,630
I was so upset I couldn't stand it.

509
00:43:59,420 --> 00:44:05,024
My second daughter didn't want
me at her wedding.

510
00:44:05,719 --> 00:44:08,969
She told the in-laws I was dead.

511
00:44:09,552 --> 00:44:11,469
What? Really?

512
00:44:12,177 --> 00:44:13,469
What a rotten girl.

513
00:44:14,852 --> 00:44:16,302
Did you just insult my daughter?

514
00:44:17,020 --> 00:44:20,382
Fair enough. You have every reason
to drown in a dish.

515
00:44:21,095 --> 00:44:22,170
What a rotten boy.

516
00:44:23,719 --> 00:44:25,561
Did you just insult my son?

517
00:44:26,520 --> 00:44:28,277
You insulted mine first.

518
00:44:28,302 --> 00:44:31,417
Sounds like you should be drowning
in a dish right beside me.

519
00:44:32,207 --> 00:44:34,230
Why are you suddenly talking down to me?

520
00:44:34,255 --> 00:44:38,052
When someone younger gets cheeky,
my words shorten on their own. Why?

521
00:44:38,511 --> 00:44:39,809
How old are you?

522
00:44:39,977 --> 00:44:41,876
You look five years younger than me. Why?

523
00:44:41,901 --> 00:44:45,216
Look who's talking.
You look ten years younger. How dare you.

524
00:44:45,469 --> 00:44:46,600
Show me your ID.

525
00:44:46,704 --> 00:44:49,246
Fine. You think I won't?

526
00:44:51,995 --> 00:44:54,266
See? I'm two years older.

527
00:44:57,302 --> 00:45:00,507
That's impossible. How can this face...

528
00:45:01,344 --> 00:45:03,372
I'd believe you were in your forties.

529
00:45:03,427 --> 00:45:06,039
Isn't this fraud? Well?

530
00:45:06,844 --> 00:45:10,018
How can anyone look this young?

531
00:45:10,877 --> 00:45:12,221
Is looking young a crime?

532
00:45:13,451 --> 00:45:16,732
Get cheeky with me again, and you're done.

533
00:45:17,632 --> 00:45:19,186
- Yes, ma'am.
- Understood?

534
00:45:19,779 --> 00:45:20,820
Yes, ma'am.

535
00:45:22,228 --> 00:45:23,409
You must be busy.

536
00:45:24,594 --> 00:45:25,636
It's fine.

537
00:45:26,261 --> 00:45:29,261
After I left your office
like that the other day,

538
00:45:30,761 --> 00:45:32,552
it kept weighing on my mind.

539
00:45:33,938 --> 00:45:37,527
I wondered if I'd spoken
only from my own point of view.

540
00:45:40,177 --> 00:45:42,892
That doesn't mean
you'll come to my wedding.

541
00:45:47,764 --> 00:45:48,814
Take this.

542
00:45:50,562 --> 00:45:53,164
- What is it?
- A wedding gift.

543
00:45:54,761 --> 00:45:56,795
Paying off your guilt with money?

544
00:45:58,619 --> 00:46:01,707
Well, open it and see if it covers it.

545
00:46:07,219 --> 00:46:09,364
(Cashier's Check, 100,000 Dollars)

546
00:46:12,761 --> 00:46:15,674
- Does my mother know?
- No.

547
00:46:16,790 --> 00:46:20,838
And this has nothing to do with her.
I'm giving it because I want to.

548
00:46:24,984 --> 00:46:27,214
You really are rich, aren't you?

549
00:46:28,094 --> 00:46:30,485
Handing over 100,000 dollars
as a wedding gift.

550
00:46:31,612 --> 00:46:35,634
Gyu Yeong, I said this to you once.

551
00:46:36,755 --> 00:46:39,973
If you're my wife's daughter,
you're my child too.

552
00:46:41,134 --> 00:46:42,134
That's right.

553
00:46:43,044 --> 00:46:48,695
Someday, when your feelings
toward your mother soften...

554
00:46:49,701 --> 00:46:51,869
I'd love for you to visit the house.

555
00:46:52,449 --> 00:46:55,440
I could introduce you to Seo Hyeon,

556
00:46:57,094 --> 00:46:59,773
and I'd like to meet your sister
and your brother too.

557
00:47:02,552 --> 00:47:04,567
Someday. No rush.

558
00:47:07,136 --> 00:47:08,335
This is so irritating.

559
00:47:11,151 --> 00:47:14,382
I'm so envious of your daughter,

560
00:47:15,596 --> 00:47:17,901
so jealous, and it irritates me.

561
00:47:18,770 --> 00:47:20,758
Why aren't you my father?

562
00:47:21,087 --> 00:47:24,540
Why is my father such a mess,
and you so wonderful?

563
00:47:25,597 --> 00:47:27,125
It really gets on my nerves.

564
00:47:29,358 --> 00:47:30,469
So irritating.

565
00:47:36,844 --> 00:47:39,937
Don't follow me. Because of you...

566
00:47:42,552 --> 00:47:44,676
I miss Kim Mu Jin so much.

567
00:48:09,721 --> 00:48:10,864
Mu Jin.

568
00:48:13,261 --> 00:48:14,664
Are you feeling all right?

569
00:48:15,136 --> 00:48:17,386
Yes, completely healed.

570
00:48:17,552 --> 00:48:18,927
Perfectly normal.

571
00:48:19,886 --> 00:48:22,444
Really? That's good.

572
00:48:24,895 --> 00:48:28,812
I can't see you for a while.

573
00:48:29,136 --> 00:48:32,527
Mom says if I see you,
I'm no longer her daughter.

574
00:48:32,594 --> 00:48:34,261
She really holds a grudge.

575
00:48:35,552 --> 00:48:36,552
I'm sorry.

576
00:48:37,261 --> 00:48:40,594
My mother is being so strange.
Just give me a little more time.

577
00:48:41,094 --> 00:48:43,890
I waited 23 years for you,
ever since I was ten.

578
00:48:43,915 --> 00:48:46,223
So wait for me a little while too.

579
00:48:47,241 --> 00:48:49,413
It won't take 23 years, I promise.

580
00:48:50,484 --> 00:48:52,683
- Seo Hyeon.
- Yes.

581
00:48:56,930 --> 00:48:59,250
What? What are you going to say?

582
00:49:03,358 --> 00:49:06,891
Something feels off.
I don't want to hear it.

583
00:49:07,235 --> 00:49:09,333
Let's hang up. I need the bathroom.

584
00:49:09,719 --> 00:49:12,009
- Seo Hyeon.
- Bye. I love you.

585
00:49:12,094 --> 00:49:15,235
I love you most on this earth. Bye.

586
00:49:26,511 --> 00:49:29,219
You have a visitor.

587
00:49:29,922 --> 00:49:33,033
- Who?
- Han Gyeol.

588
00:49:36,826 --> 00:49:39,060
Tell him I'm out. That I didn't come in.

589
00:49:39,880 --> 00:49:41,719
That's what I meant to do,

590
00:49:42,208 --> 00:49:45,518
but why is it I can't lie to children?

591
00:49:48,312 --> 00:49:50,745
Say you thought I was in, but I'm not.

592
00:49:52,109 --> 00:49:54,067
Fine. Got it.

593
00:49:54,213 --> 00:49:58,010
Drawing the line here
is the right thing for Gyeol too.

594
00:49:58,610 --> 00:50:01,938
I'll do my best to lie for you.

595
00:50:18,087 --> 00:50:19,260
Gyeol.

596
00:50:21,187 --> 00:50:22,540
Mu Jin.

597
00:50:36,793 --> 00:50:38,602
- Is it good?
- Yes.

598
00:50:47,020 --> 00:50:48,320
I'm relieved.

599
00:50:49,626 --> 00:50:50,626
About what?

600
00:50:50,846 --> 00:50:53,333
I came to see you one last time,

601
00:50:53,561 --> 00:50:55,426
and I got to see you after all.

602
00:50:56,821 --> 00:50:57,861
Last time?

603
00:50:58,494 --> 00:51:02,040
I don't think I should
come see you anymore.

604
00:51:04,101 --> 00:51:05,407
Did your mother...

605
00:51:12,701 --> 00:51:14,109
I feel the same way too.

606
00:51:14,868 --> 00:51:17,829
- In sync to the very end.
- I knew it.

607
00:51:20,747 --> 00:51:24,780
Should we shake hands one last time
before we say goodbye?

608
00:51:25,620 --> 00:51:27,177
Before we shake hands,

609
00:51:28,258 --> 00:51:30,466
there's one last thing I want to say.

610
00:51:32,612 --> 00:51:33,626
What is it?

611
00:51:33,699 --> 00:51:37,119
Because I don't want to lie to you.

612
00:51:39,787 --> 00:51:44,407
My mom and Cho Heung Sik
aren't married yet.

613
00:51:47,059 --> 00:51:50,412
I know. I heard not long ago.

614
00:51:50,634 --> 00:51:54,383
You knew? Then why
didn't you say anything?

615
00:51:58,981 --> 00:52:02,274
Because I wanted to respect her decision.

616
00:52:03,388 --> 00:52:07,074
The lie was her decision too.

617
00:52:08,426 --> 00:52:13,706
But she did propose to Cho Heung Sik.

618
00:52:15,846 --> 00:52:16,888
Did she?

619
00:52:18,724 --> 00:52:19,786
I see.

620
00:52:22,834 --> 00:52:25,767
Let's shake hands now, one last time.

621
00:52:29,787 --> 00:52:32,617
Take care, Gyeol. Stay healthy.

622
00:52:32,894 --> 00:52:35,424
You take care and stay healthy too.

623
00:53:13,434 --> 00:53:15,278
What? Who? Han Gyu O?

624
00:53:15,567 --> 00:53:18,471
Yes. A friend of my boyfriend's friend.

625
00:53:18,687 --> 00:53:20,020
You don't know him?

626
00:53:20,513 --> 00:53:23,699
The way he looked at your photo
told a whole story.

627
00:53:26,406 --> 00:53:28,018
He's not a stalker, is he?

628
00:53:28,233 --> 00:53:30,221
Did I speak up for nothing?

629
00:53:31,382 --> 00:53:32,540
So?

630
00:53:33,393 --> 00:53:35,586
I only showed him your photo.

631
00:53:35,714 --> 00:53:38,600
I never gave him your number
or your Instagram.

632
00:53:39,459 --> 00:53:42,497
He's really good-looking, though.

633
00:53:42,522 --> 00:53:43,915
Totally my type.

634
00:53:44,127 --> 00:53:46,816
If he weren't tied to you,
I'd have snatched him myself.

635
00:53:51,207 --> 00:53:52,991
Han Gyu O asked me to tell you this.

636
00:53:53,016 --> 00:53:56,185
He'll be waiting at Haeoreum Park
at eight tonight,

637
00:53:56,263 --> 00:53:58,304
so come if you want to see him.

638
00:53:58,330 --> 00:53:59,627
He said he'd wait.

639
00:53:59,994 --> 00:54:02,911
I sent his number to your chat.

640
00:54:11,967 --> 00:54:13,880
Tell me if you're not going.

641
00:54:15,080 --> 00:54:17,013
If you don't want him, I'll go.

642
00:54:54,913 --> 00:54:56,326
Looks like a total gigolo.

643
00:55:32,648 --> 00:55:34,398
- Just a moment, please.
- Yes.

644
00:55:45,205 --> 00:55:46,705
(Han Gyu O)

645
00:55:48,268 --> 00:55:49,688
(Copied.)

646
00:55:50,952 --> 00:55:52,872
(Paste)

647
00:55:52,978 --> 00:55:56,551
(That gigolo)

648
00:55:56,620 --> 00:55:58,127
Why is this guy's number coming up?

649
00:56:03,888 --> 00:56:05,294
(Copy text)

650
00:56:05,852 --> 00:56:07,372
(Paste)

651
00:56:07,423 --> 00:56:10,474
(That gigolo)

652
00:56:12,347 --> 00:56:16,108
Why is Han Gyu O's number
the same as that gigolo's?

653
00:56:17,183 --> 00:56:22,106
Han Gyu O was the gigolo?

654
00:57:34,627 --> 00:57:37,773
Was anything turned in
to lost and found yesterday?

655
00:57:38,207 --> 00:57:40,722
Someone claimed a phone earlier,

656
00:57:41,013 --> 00:57:42,887
and a hat was picked up just now.

657
00:57:43,275 --> 00:57:44,666
What is it you lost?

658
00:57:45,467 --> 00:57:48,220
I'm not really sure what it is.

659
00:57:49,380 --> 00:57:50,380
Sorry?

660
00:57:50,860 --> 00:57:53,961
I know that sounds absurd,

661
00:57:54,384 --> 00:57:56,667
but I definitely lost something.

662
00:57:58,287 --> 00:58:02,281
So you lost something,

663
00:58:02,615 --> 00:58:06,613
but you don't know what it was you lost?

664
00:58:07,407 --> 00:58:08,427
Yes.

665
00:58:08,863 --> 00:58:12,707
Then leave your number or a business card.

666
00:58:12,732 --> 00:58:15,397
If anything turns up, I'll call or text.

667
00:58:15,952 --> 00:58:17,469
Thank you.

668
00:58:28,481 --> 00:58:31,335
So I came out this way...

669
00:58:35,074 --> 00:58:37,483
and walked like this, didn't I?

670
00:58:43,674 --> 00:58:46,955
Gyu Rim, what's this?

671
00:58:47,393 --> 00:58:49,879
Someone helped me.

672
00:58:51,086 --> 00:58:53,525
Thank you. Good night.

673
00:59:10,904 --> 00:59:12,938
Thank you.

674
00:59:21,220 --> 00:59:22,511
Who was it?

675
00:59:37,086 --> 00:59:38,893
Who on earth were you?

676
01:00:10,283 --> 01:00:12,373
Chef, did you burn your hand?

677
01:00:12,420 --> 01:00:14,133
I'll get the first aid kit.

678
01:00:19,246 --> 01:00:20,873
Just this once.

679
01:00:21,394 --> 01:00:23,343
From how you helped with closing,

680
01:00:23,677 --> 01:00:26,046
you're quick, you're sorry,

681
01:00:26,227 --> 01:00:27,879
and you're trying. That's commendable.

682
01:00:27,904 --> 01:00:29,676
So I'm letting it slide just this once.

683
01:00:29,701 --> 01:00:30,823
Thank you.

684
01:00:30,970 --> 01:00:34,420
I'll never be even one second late again.

685
01:00:42,373 --> 01:00:43,393
Gyu Min?

686
01:00:44,846 --> 01:00:46,379
It's you, isn't it?

687
01:00:47,892 --> 01:00:49,586
What is this, you two?

688
01:00:51,633 --> 01:00:56,223
So how do you two know each other?

689
01:00:57,337 --> 01:01:00,075
It can't be, can it?

690
01:01:01,629 --> 01:01:04,636
That's right. Gyu Rim's sister.

691
01:01:07,647 --> 01:01:11,613
- This was your place?
- Yes.

692
01:01:12,742 --> 01:01:14,833
So you're the new part-timer.

693
01:01:15,481 --> 01:01:16,550
Yes.

694
01:01:17,844 --> 01:01:19,507
I'll do my best.

695
01:01:20,714 --> 01:01:23,120
Same here. Let's work well together.

696
01:01:25,096 --> 01:01:28,890
Gyu O said Gyu Rim lost something
and can't find it.

697
01:01:29,014 --> 01:01:31,517
That's why I helped look for it
and ended up late.

698
01:01:31,620 --> 01:01:34,221
What is it? What did she lose?

699
01:01:34,781 --> 01:01:35,784
That's just it.

700
01:01:35,912 --> 01:01:38,487
Nobody knows, and that's
exactly what's maddening.

701
01:01:38,727 --> 01:01:42,160
It's hard enough when we know what it is.
How can we find what we don't know?

702
01:01:42,867 --> 01:01:45,487
Did she hit her head somewhere
on the way home, drunk?

703
01:01:47,100 --> 01:01:49,880
Right? I thought the same thing.

704
01:01:50,587 --> 01:01:54,828
What if some mugger hit her
on the head and something's wrong?

705
01:01:54,862 --> 01:01:56,347
What do we do then?

706
01:01:56,627 --> 01:01:57,773
Anyway, I'll see you at home.

707
01:01:57,806 --> 01:01:59,559
This is no small problem.

708
01:02:01,307 --> 01:02:03,866
Got it. I'll be there soon.

709
01:02:07,622 --> 01:02:08,820
You startled me.

710
01:02:10,334 --> 01:02:13,067
Is something wrong with Gyu Rim?

711
01:02:30,873 --> 01:02:32,893
Did you find what you lost?

712
01:02:36,921 --> 01:02:39,077
I heard you lost something while drinking.

713
01:02:40,391 --> 01:02:41,474
Did you find it?

714
01:02:42,547 --> 01:02:44,127
How do you know about...

715
01:02:48,814 --> 01:02:49,833
No.

716
01:02:52,087 --> 01:02:54,013
Not even a clue?

717
01:02:56,847 --> 01:02:57,979
It's all right.

718
01:02:59,080 --> 01:03:00,540
Don't worry about it.

719
01:03:01,007 --> 01:03:02,713
Did you check the bar?

720
01:03:04,220 --> 01:03:07,011
Nothing dropped at the convenience store,

721
01:03:07,119 --> 01:03:10,213
the crosswalk, or anywhere along the way.

722
01:03:11,087 --> 01:03:13,747
How do you know about the store
and the crosswalk...

723
01:03:23,466 --> 01:03:25,066
Gyu Rim. Han Gyu Rim.

724
01:03:25,273 --> 01:03:26,493
Gyu Rim!

725
01:03:37,453 --> 01:03:38,949
You can't just cross like that.

726
01:03:38,974 --> 01:03:40,213
Do you want to get killed?

727
01:03:41,322 --> 01:03:42,687
It was you, Mu Jin.

728
01:03:50,860 --> 01:03:52,213
Is your stomach all right?

729
01:04:17,309 --> 01:04:19,697
What do I do?

730
01:04:28,713 --> 01:04:30,713
This can't be happening.

731
01:04:32,556 --> 01:04:34,763
It came back to me.

732
01:04:35,273 --> 01:04:37,893
What it was that I lost,

733
01:04:38,809 --> 01:04:41,504
it came back to me. What do I do?

734
01:04:46,297 --> 01:04:48,517
What am I going to do?

735
01:05:19,033 --> 01:05:21,439
(Love on the Menu)

736
01:05:21,464 --> 01:05:23,993
I'm sorry I ran away from you.

737
01:05:24,150 --> 01:05:26,913
I'm sorry I gave you up.

738
01:05:26,960 --> 01:05:29,764
You and I are done being man and woman.

739
01:05:29,789 --> 01:05:32,999
If Seo Hyeon runs away, will you take her
into your arms?

740
01:05:33,024 --> 01:05:36,658
You're fired. Your paycheck is gone.

741
01:05:36,689 --> 01:05:38,238
Give me Han Gyu O.

742
01:05:38,263 --> 01:05:41,317
No. Anyone else, but never you.

743
01:05:41,407 --> 01:05:43,166
It's been a long time, Gyu Rim.

744
01:05:43,348 --> 01:05:44,914
I'm sorry I didn't reach out.

745
01:05:44,939 --> 01:05:46,578
I wasn't going to call,

746
01:05:46,603 --> 01:05:48,957
but I missed you too much.

747
01:05:48,982 --> 01:05:50,982
Am I that easy to push around?

748
01:05:52,097 --> 01:05:53,897
Dramaday.me
